-- Lesson 8: Regional Dialects Mastery
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## Major Oromo Dialect Zones

Afaan Oromoo is mutually intelligible across regions but shows systematic variation. Advanced speakers recognize the dialect from the first sentence.

| Zone | Example region |
|------|---------------|
| Borana | Southern Oromia, Kenya |
| Guji | Guji zone |
| Arsi | Arsi zone |
| Wollega | Western Oromia |
| Shewa | Central Oromia |
| Hararghe | Eastern Oromia |

## Key Variation Patterns

| Feature | Borana | Shewa | Wollega |
|---------|--------|-------|---------|
| "Now" | amma | ammuma | ammaan |
| "Come" | kottu | kootu | kootu |
| Vowel laxing | minimal | moderate | strong |

## Lexical Differences

| Meaning | Borana | Wollega |
|---------|--------|---------|
| bread | daabboo | buddeena |
| home | mana | manaa |
| water | bishaan | bishaan |

## Tips for Mastery

- Listen to regional radio: OBN (Shewa), Borana FM, Dhageettii Wollega
- Note phonetic shifts: Borana preserves older forms; Shewa shows Amharic contact
- Respect regional identity; don't "correct" native dialects

**Practice tip:** Pick one dialect to produce actively, but train your ear to receive all of them.
$CONTENT$
