-- Lesson 9: Professional Discourse
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## Oromo in Professional Settings

Professional contexts — meetings, emails, reports — require clarity, brevity, and respectful tone. Formal Afaan Oromoo is increasingly used in government, media, healthcare, and NGOs in Oromia.

| Setting | Register Features |
|---------|-------------------|
| Meeting | Honorifics, turn-taking, concise claims |
| Email | Greeting, subject, clear request, sign-off |
| Report | Structured headings, data-supported claims |
| Interview | Measured pace, full answers |

## Email Template (Oromo)

**Subject:** Gabaasa Hojii — Sadaasa 2024
**Greeting:** Kabajamoo Obbo/Aadde [Maqaa],
**Body:** Gabaasni hojii ji'a Sadaasa kana argamee jira.
**Close:** Galatoomaa, [Maqaa keessanii]

## Meeting Vocabulary

| Oromo | English |
|-------|---------|
| walgahii | meeting |
| murtii | decision |
| gaaffii | question |
| deebii | answer |
| akeeka | agenda |

## Telephone and Video Calls

Open with full greeting (*Akkam jirtu?*), identify yourself, state purpose in one sentence, listen actively, close with gratitude.

**Practice tip:** Draft professional emails in Oromo, then have a native speaker review for register.
$CONTENT$
