-- Lesson 10: Mastery Assessment
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## Capstone of Advanced Afaan Oromoo

This final lesson integrates morphology, syntax, register, literary analysis, and professional discourse. A C2 learner should be able to produce, read, and critique a wide range of texts.

## Assessment Dimensions

| Skill | What to demonstrate |
|-------|---------------------|
| Reading | Understand news, literature, academic prose |
| Writing | Produce essays, reports, creative pieces |
| Listening | Follow OBN news, regional broadcasts, poetry |
| Speaking | Debate, present, narrate in multiple registers |
| Cultural | Navigate *safuu*, honorifics, idioms |

## Capstone Tasks

1. Summarize a 1,000-word news article into 200 words in Oromo.
2. Translate a proverb-rich folktale into English preserving cultural force.
3. Deliver a 5-minute speech on *Gadaa* for a mixed audience.
4. Draft a formal complaint letter in Oromo.
5. Analyze a Hachalu Hundessa lyric for theme and voice.

## Self-Check Rubric

| Dimension | Beginner | Intermediate | Advanced |
|-----------|----------|--------------|----------|
| Vocabulary | 500 words | 3,000 | 10,000+ |
| Errors | Frequent | Occasional | Rare |
| Register | One | Two | All |

## Beyond Mastery

Language mastery is lifelong. Continue reading, listening, conversing, and writing. Contribute to Wikipedia Afaan Oromoo, translate works, and mentor new learners.

**Final takeaway:** A language is a people's soul. Honoring Afaan Oromoo is honoring the Oromo nation.
$CONTENT$
