-- Lesson 8: Saying Goodbye
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## Goodbye! 👋

When we leave, we say **nagaatti** (goodbye) in Oromo.

| Oromo | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| nagaatti | goodbye |
| booda walitti | see you later |
| bor walitti | see you tomorrow |
| galatoomi | thank you |
| baga hawwatte | you are welcome |
| galgala gaarii | good evening |
| halkan gaarii | good night |

## Goodbye Chat

**Friend:** Nagaatti!
**You:** Nagaatti! Bor walitti! 👋

## Before Bed

Say **halkan gaarii** to your family before bed. Sweet dreams! 🌙

**You've done it!** You finished the Afaan Oromoo for Kids course! Great work! 🎉🎉

**Today you learned:** How to say goodbye, thank you, and good night in Oromo.
