-- ================= COURSE: ali-birra-music (8 lessons) =================

-- Lesson 1: Young Ali in Dire Dawa
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## A Boy from Dire Dawa

Ali Mohammed Musa, known to the world as **Ali Birra**, was born on September 18, 1950 in Dire Dawa, an ancient railway city in eastern Ethiopia. The name *Birra* — meaning "spring" or "blossom" in Afaan Oromoo — became part of his artistic identity.

| Fact | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Birth name | Ali Mohammed Musa |
| Stage name | Ali Birra |
| Born | September 18, 1950 |
| Birthplace | Dire Dawa, Ethiopia |
| Language | Afaan Oromoo |

## A Multicultural City

Dire Dawa brought together Oromo, Somali, Amhara, Harari, and Arab communities. Young Ali grew up hearing many musics at once — traditional Oromo songs, Harari *zikr*, Somali poetry, Egyptian classics on radio. This mix shaped his ear.

## Early Musical Hunger

By his teens, Ali was performing at weddings and cultural events, learning rhythm from traditional Oromo *shaggoyyee* and melody from neighborhood singers. Afaan Oromoo music was not yet welcomed on state radio, but the streets of Dire Dawa nurtured it.

**Key takeaway:** Ali's Dire Dawa childhood gave him the cultural blend and persistence that would define his life in music.
$CONTENT$
