-- Lesson 7: Later Career and Recognition
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## A Long, Honored Career

Ali Birra continued performing and recording well into the 2000s and 2010s, adapting to new formats while remaining faithful to Afaan Oromoo.

## Honors

| Honor | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| Honorary Doctorate | Jimma University |
| Cultural ambassador | Widely invoked title |
| Lifetime achievement awards | Multiple Ethiopian and diaspora bodies |
| National mourning | Following his death in 2022 |

## Studio Work

Ali adopted modern production techniques — digital recording, music videos, international collaborations — without losing his signature warmth. His albums found new listeners on YouTube and Oromo-language streaming channels.

## Collaboration

He appeared with younger artists, blessing their careers on stage and in recordings. This practice mirrored the Oromo tradition of *seera-keenya* — passing knowledge from elders to youth.

## Final Years

In November 2022, after a long illness, Ali Birra passed away on November 6, 2022. The Oromo community and Ethiopia mourned. Government officials and cultural institutions organized tributes.

**Key takeaway:** Ali did not retire from Oromo music — he remained an active voice until the end, and the community returned his decades of service with deep respect.
$CONTENT$
