-- Lesson 6: The 2016 Bishoftu Tragedy
UPDATE public.lessons SET content = $CONTENT$## A Festival Shadowed

On October 2, 2016, during the Irreecha festival at Hora Harsadi near Bishoftu, a catastrophic stampede and violence resulted in many deaths. The event is remembered as one of the most tragic moments in modern Oromo history.

## What Happened

During the festival, tensions between security forces and protesters escalated. Crowd panic led to a stampede; many people were trampled or injured in steep terrain around the lake. Some were killed in the ensuing chaos.

## Casualty Figures

Official Ethiopian figures reported dozens of deaths; opposition and community sources reported much higher numbers, sometimes in the hundreds. The true toll remains disputed. Many more were injured.

## Context

The tragedy occurred during the height of the 2014-2018 Oromo protests. Irreecha had become a site not only of thanksgiving but of political expression. Tensions between state security and protesters had been building for months.

## Mourning

The incident prompted widespread grief across Oromia and the diaspora. Families remain unable to locate some loved ones. Annual remembrances are held.

## Irreecha Since 2016

The festival has continued, with increased security and complex management. Many participants honor the victims during the celebration.

## Memory Work

Documenting the tragedy, supporting affected families, and seeking accountability remain ongoing. Oromo activists, journalists, and scholars have worked to preserve testimony.

## A Caution

This topic is painful for many Oromo families. Treat it with gravity — not spectacle.

**Key takeaway:** The October 2, 2016 Bishoftu tragedy remains a painful moment in Oromo history; remembering it honestly is part of Irreecha's complex modern meaning.
$CONTENT$
